{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## /rebar-debug — Final report (RESOLVED, merged)\n\n**Problem.** The on-box MCP image shipped without the `acli` (Atlassian CLI) binary, so every\nJira-**mutating** bridge op (`bridge_check_access`, `reconcile`) died at the transport with\n`[Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'acli'` at `STEP_CREATE`. Direct-REST paths were unaffected;\ncredentials/connectivity/scope were already proven good.\n\n**Proven root cause.** `infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp` had no `acli` install step. The Jira\ntransport spawns `acli` by bare name (`_DEFAULT_ACLI_CMD = [\"acli\"]` ->\n`subprocess.Popen(full_cmd)` in `adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py`, no `which`/abs-path guard), so\nan absent binary raises `FileNotFoundError`, surfaced verbatim by `access_check.py:237-241`.\n\n**Proof.** `grep -rn \"acli|atlassian\" infra/compose/Dockerfile.*` -> nothing. Runtime repro of the\nexact string: `Popen(['acli'], env={'PATH':'/nonexistent'})` -> `[Errno 2] No such file or\ndirectory: 'acli'`. Discriminates against the already-excluded rivals (creds `GET /myself`->200,\nconnectivity, scope).\n\n**Escalation -> resolved as MECHANICAL fix (no unilateral adoption).** `acli` is already an\naccepted, pinned rebar dependency -- README, `docs/jira-sync-setup.md` (`ACLI_VERSION=1.3.19-stable`\n+ `ACLI_SHA256`), CI `.github/workflows/external-integration.yml` (download+verify+install). It is\npublic/free (both arch tarballs downloaded anonymously, no license/account), a single ~15 MB static\nbinary in a ~6 MB tarball. Per /rebar-debug Step 5 this is the \"already-accepted dependency the\nimage omits\" case, not a new external dependency -> proceed.\n\n**Defect origin.** Commit `8297083532a3` (ticket `fd4a-4e91-f179-4932`, \"Add rebar-mcp HTTP service\nto the AWS box\") introduced `Dockerfile.mcp` but never provisioned the bridge's `acli` transport.\nMasked until `colourless-hasteless-lamb` wired credentials and moved the probe past its credential\ngate. Close: `caused_by=fd4a-4e91-f179-4932`, class `plan_defect`.\n\n**Test (RED->GREEN).** `tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py::test_dockerfile_mcp_provisions_pinned_acli_on_path`\nasserts the image declares the pinned, arch-aware, sha256-verified install (host `acli.atlassian.com`,\n`ACLI_VERSION`!=latest, `TARGETARCH`, >=2 distinct 64-hex per-arch shas, `sha256sum -c`,\n`/usr/local/bin/acli`). Confirmed RED before the fix; GREEN after; mutation-checked (deleting the\ninstall block turns it RED).\n\n**Fix.** `Dockerfile.mcp`: after the OpenSSH RUN, a build step selects arch via Docker `TARGETARCH`,\ndownloads `acli_${ACLI_VERSION}_linux_{amd64,arm64}.tar.gz`, `sha256sum -c --strict` against the\nper-arch pin, extracts only the `acli` binary and `install -m 0755` to `/usr/local/bin/acli`,\nsmoke-checks `acli --version`, then purges curl and apt lists. amd64 `f29fa8b7...383a6d`,\narm64 `72972e74...3674da` for `1.3.19-stable`.\n\n**Scope & safety / portability.** Deploy box is AL2023 **arm64** (`docker-compose.yml:4`) but CI\ndownloads amd64 -- the fix is arch-aware so it ships an executable binary on the box. It is a plain\nDockerfile step with no CI/deploy-system coupling -> satisfies `project.portability`. No credentials\nused at build time; no secrets in the diff.\n\n**Siblings.** Only the `mcp` container runs Jira-mutating bridge ops (review-bot is code-review\nonly) -- no sibling images need the same fix.\n\n**Residual risk.** `access_check.py` STEP_CREATE still surfaces a raw `FileNotFoundError` string\nrather than a typed \"transport unavailable\" verdict; hardening tracked as follow-up\n`naval-cankered-stud` (ac93-8afd-1666-4866), linked discovered_from this ticket.\n\n**Replication.** Native-arch `docker build` of the acli layer resolves `acli --version` at\n`/usr/local/bin/acli`; the pre-fix base image reproduces the `FileNotFoundError`.\n\n**Landed.** Gerrit change **2370** (Change-Id `I4a07c1adb1e4ce70c35753491e5abe2a0864c082`),\nPS2: LLM-Review +1 (PASS, advisory-only) + Verified +1 (CI success) -> **Submitted/MERGED** as\n`f056344f928d`. Ticket closed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788026262746605001,"uuid":"23dde0a9-e9e5-4606-bdc3-0c14660edb2e"}